migrations/0003_drops.sql:1:1: DROP TABLE deletes data
  fix: if that is intended, put "-- maago: allow-drop" on the line right before it
migrations/0003_drops.sql:2:1: ALTER TABLE … DROP COLUMN deletes data
  fix: if the column was renamed, delete the file and run maago makemigrations --rename TABLE.OLD:NEW; if losing it is intended, put "-- maago: allow-drop" on the line right before it
migrations/0003_drops.sql:3:1: ALTER TABLE … DROP COLUMN deletes data
  fix: if the column was renamed, delete the file and run maago makemigrations --rename TABLE.OLD:NEW; if losing it is intended, put "-- maago: allow-drop" on the line right before it
migrations/0003_drops.sql:4:1: ALTER TABLE … DROP COLUMN deletes data
  fix: if the column was renamed, delete the file and run maago makemigrations --rename TABLE.OLD:NEW; if losing it is intended, put "-- maago: allow-drop" on the line right before it
migrations/0003_drops.sql:5:1: -- maago: allow-drop is not before a DROP TABLE or DROP COLUMN statement
  fix: remove it, or move it to the line right before the DROP
